Subject: [PATCH 399/443] [ae-patch] Voice mode on iPhone: release the cloud
 audio element before the mic starts

On WebKit, after a cloud reply plays through the shared audio element, the element kept holding the iOS audio session, so every later recognizer heard nothing ("No speech detected") until Voice ended. The cloud speaker now fully releases the element (pause, no src, load) on a stop, a barge-in and a play error as well as when the queue drains, and the mic start (whenSynthIdle, which also covers the approval phase) asks the speaker to release first and waits a named 150 ms settle (MIC_AUDIO_SETTLE_MS) before the recognizer starts. A reply that is still speaking is never released, the element instance is kept so the tap-unlock stays, and the next sentence sets src again. Non-WebKit is unchanged.
